  "notes": "Boot a Corvette ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released); the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM FACTORY SETTINGS RESTORED loop with Escape (5), press Enter twice (game identification, then MAIN MENU), Up twice to T. TESTS and Enter to open the test menu at T.1 SWITCH EDGES. Open T.16 ZR1-LT5 TEST, whose SELF TEST runs on entry; the display shows the engine position, the FULL LEFT and FULL RIGHT optos and the edges it found. Then select AUTO RUN, ENGINE LEFT, ENGINE RIGHT and ENGINE CENTER in turn with Up and start each with Enter, watching each for 10 s (Escape would leave the test). Run once with PinMAME's built-in engine mechanism (--handle-mechanics 7), which sets 71 below position 64 and 72 above 191 from the ROM's engine-position register, and once without it (--handle-mechanics 0), so nothing answers the ROM and the self test fails.",
  "version": 1
}
